WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:05.769
You saw the exact payload each ISC
workflow sends, and the intended state

3
00:00:05.769 --> 00:00:10.662
each finding carries: a native change
reverted, an attribute change kept.

4
00:00:10.662 --> 00:00:15.565
You saw the two fixes that keep a finding
from reaching the re-read with nothing to

5
00:00:15.565 --> 00:00:18.565
check: multivalued changes
now sent and reverted,

6
00:00:18.565 --> 00:00:21.199
and the attribute in
the de-duplication key.

7
00:00:21.199 --> 00:00:23.934
And you confirmed that
a closure signal moves a

8
00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:27.088
finding to Awaiting verification
but never closes it.

9
00:00:27.088 --> 00:00:30.762
Before shipping, work through
the Chapter 04 checklist.

10
00:00:30.762 --> 00:00:36.217
Next is Module 6, actuation and the
re-read rule: how Gate 5 actuates by lane,

11
00:00:36.217 --> 00:00:39.307
and how Gate 6 closes
a finding only when a

12
00:00:39.307 --> 00:00:42.762
re-read of the target
shows the intended state.

13
00:00:42.762 --> 00:00:47.060
You'll watch the re-read client decide
six waiting findings on two days.
